export const verifiedQuestionCatalog = [{"id":"offline-sync","category":"accounts-sync","question":"Can I use ProgressTracker without internet?","aliases":["What happens when I go offline?","Will my changes sync later?","Can I use this without internet?"],"keywords":["offline","local","sync","internet","device"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/db/localRepository.ts","src/services/supabase/syncEngine.ts","src/features/auth/AuthProvider.tsx"],"answer":"Tracker data is stored locally in the browser, so you can continue working while offline. Signed-in account data synchronizes when a connection is available again. Until then, changes on that device may not appear elsewhere."},{"id":"cross-device-sync","category":"accounts-sync","question":"Will my progress appear on another device?","aliases":["How do I sync trackers between devices?","Can I access my data on a new device?"],"keywords":["account","sign in","sync","devices","cloud"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/auth/AuthProvider.tsx","src/services/supabase/syncEngine.ts"],"answer":"Cross-device synchronization is available when you sign in to the same account and the devices are online. Guest data is stored locally on the device and does not automatically appear on another device."},{"id":"sync-conflicts","category":"accounts-sync","question":"What happens if two devices edit the same day?","aliases":["How does sync handle conflicting edits?","Will ProgressTracker merge two versions automatically?"],"keywords":["conflict","revision","sync","devices","edit"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/services/supabase/syncEngine.ts","src/db/syncConflictRepository.ts","src/db/syncConflictRepository.test.ts","src/db/syncRecoveryRepository.ts","src/db/syncRecoveryRepository.test.ts","src/db/trackerRecoveryPreview.ts","src/features/auth/AuthPage.tsx","src/features/auth/AuthPage.test.tsx","src/features/auth/BlockedTrackerSyncCard.tsx","src/features/auth/TrackerRecoveryPreview.tsx"],"answer":"When two saved versions have different cloud revisions, sync preserves the local and cloud copies and asks you to review them under Account → Sync conflicts. Choose which version to keep, or save the local record under a new ID when no cloud record is readable. Permanent server validation rejections remain blocked with their payloads and diagnostics; **Try again** is disabled for these errors, and the unchanged payload is never replayed. A transient retry first checks the local operation and current cloud revision; changed cloud state becomes a conflict. **Undo unsynced changes** is available for a tracker when its latest confirmed cloud definition can be restored safely. It previews the definition changes, validates a workspace backup before export, then asks you to save the file and confirm that you can retrieve it. The browser cannot verify the destination. Undo preserves valid independent check-ins and stops when the schema differs without a verified conversion, a measure identity or type changes unsafely, the acknowledged cloud revision is stale, or a related conflict or deletion request needs review. Guarded **Repair Changes** appears under **Other recovery options** when the preview offers a verified correction. Once you explicitly confirm permanent deletion in the Bin, deletion is authoritative for that tracker: its pending or rejected tracker and check-in writes are marked superseded locally and cannot replay. The durable deletion request works offline and retains the original Wins choice. When online, sync fetches a fresh owner-scoped cloud revision and calls the existing deletion RPC before tracker uploads; the RPC atomically deletes against that revision, so rejected settings are never uploaded and no repair or backup is required. If another device changes the tracker during the request, the revision check reports the conflict and the saved deletion retries against a fresh revision. Local tracker and check-in data remain hidden and retained until the server confirms deletion. After confirmation, local content and recovery conflicts are cleared, minimal payload-free operation diagnostics remain, and the server deletion ledger prevents older application versions or devices from recreating the tracker."},{"id":"account-signin","category":"accounts-sync","question":"How do I sign in or create an account?","aliases":["Can I sign in with an email link?","How do I register?"],"keywords":["sign in","create account","email link","password","authentication"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/auth/AuthPage.tsx","src/features/auth/authService.ts","src/features/auth/AuthPage.test.tsx"],"answer":"Use the account screen to request an email sign-in link or choose password sign-in. Choose Create account when registering a new account; using an email sign-in link for the first time creates an account for that email."},{"id":"workspace-backup","category":"accounts-sync","question":"Can I back up or restore my workspace data?","aliases":["How do I export my progress?","Can I import a workspace backup?"],"keywords":["backup","export","restore","JSON","workspace","sync conflicts"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/auth/WorkspaceBackup.tsx","src/db/workspaceBackup.ts","src/db/workspaceBackup.test.ts"],"answer":"Settings provides a local workspace backup you can download as JSON and restore into the same guest workspace or account. Restore previews changes, adds missing records, skips identical records, and stops if it finds a conflicting ID or date. Sync operation states are preserved too: a server-rejected change remains blocked with its payload and diagnostic, an explicitly discarded change remains inert with its audit payload, and an already superseded operation remains historical; none is made retryable by restoring a backup. Keep the backup file private."},{"id":"signout-local-data","category":"accounts-sync","question":"What happens to local workspace data when I sign out?","aliases":["Does signing out erase check-ins from this device?","Will my local progress remain after sign-out?"],"keywords":["sign out","local workspace","check-ins","data","account"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/auth/AuthProvider.tsx","src/db/localRepository.ts"],"answer":"Signing out ends the account session; it does not itself delete the local workspace records. Account data remains associated with its local workspace, and the app uses a workspace-selection step when choosing guest data after sign-out."},{"id":"offline-sync-later","category":"accounts-sync","question":"What happens to a check-in I save while offline?","aliases":["Will my offline entry upload when I reconnect?","Does a disconnected check-in stay on this device?"],"keywords":["offline check-in","pending sync","reconnect","local storage"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/db/localRepository.ts","src/services/supabase/syncEngine.ts","src/features/auth/AuthProvider.tsx"],"answer":"The check-in is saved locally and its account-sync work remains pending until a connection is available. If that tracker has a blocked or conflicted definition change, the check-in stays queued until a newer definition is acknowledged. If you explicitly confirm permanently deleting the tracker, that deletion supersedes its pending tracker and check-in writes; those writes are not uploaded. The check-in may not appear on another device before synchronization completes."},{"id":"sync-deletion","category":"accounts-sync","question":"Does clearing a check-in sync to my other devices?","aliases":["Will a cleared entry disappear from my other device?","Does a check-in deletion upload when I reconnect?"],"keywords":["clear check-in","sync","other devices","deletion marker"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/db/localRepository.ts","src/services/supabase/syncEngine.ts"],"answer":"For a signed-in account, clearing queues a deletion update for synchronization. Other devices reflect the change after they synchronize with the account; while offline, they may still show their earlier local copy."},{"id":"sync-conflict-preserves-versions","category":"accounts-sync","question":"What information is kept when two device edits conflict?","aliases":["Does sync keep both versions of a conflict?","Can ProgressTracker merge conflicting tracker changes automatically?"],"keywords":["sync conflict","local version","remote version","revision","resolution"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/services/supabase/syncEngine.ts","src/db/syncConflictRepository.ts","src/db/syncConflictRepository.test.ts"],"answer":"When a revision conflict cannot be reconciled safely, the sync flow records the conflicting local and remote data for you to resolve. It does not silently blend incompatible changes. Review the conflict under Account → Sync conflicts before choosing which version to keep. If the server permanently rejects a write for validation, the local payload is retained as a blocked operation instead of being retried automatically or presented as a competing cloud version."},{"id":"sync-preference-scope","category":"accounts-sync","question":"Do workspace time zone and appearance settings sync between devices?","aliases":["Will my theme and calendar time zone follow me to another device?","Are workspace display preferences stored in my account?"],"keywords":["settings","time zone","appearance","sync","devices"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/settings/WorkspaceTimeZone.tsx","src/features/settings/appearance.ts","src/features/settings/UnifiedSettings.test.tsx"],"answer":"Appearance is stored locally on each device. A signed-in workspace's time zone is saved to the account and synchronized between devices; guest workspaces keep it locally."},{"id":"ai-help-private-data","category":"ai-help","question":"Can AI Help see my tracker entries?","aliases":["Does Groq receive my personal progress?","What data is sent when I ask a question?","Can AI Help read my check-in values?"],"keywords":["privacy","tracker entries","personal data","Groq","AI Help"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/ai-help/aiHelpService.ts","supabase/functions/ai-help/index.ts","supabase/functions/ai-help/assistantCore.ts"],"answer":"AI Help answers questions about how the product works; its request includes your question and limited conversation context, not your tracker entries. Do not include private tracker details in a question or support message."},{"id":"ai-help-suggested-offline","category":"ai-help","question":"Can I use suggested AI Help questions while offline?","aliases":["Do the suggested questions work without internet?","Can AI Help show a saved answer if I am disconnected?"],"keywords":["AI Help","suggestions","offline","verified answer","internet"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/ai-help/aiHelpService.ts","src/features/ai-help/AIHelpAssistant.tsx"],"answer":"Yes, a displayed verified suggestion opens its bundled answer without a network request. Manually typed questions need a connection for the full retrieval service; only questions matched by the smaller local help catalog can receive a local answer offline."},{"id":"ai-help-typed-retrieval","category":"ai-help","question":"How does AI Help handle a question I type myself?","aliases":["Does free-form Ask ProgressTracker use the verified answers?","What happens when I ask a question that is not a suggestion?"],"keywords":["AI Help","typed question","free-form","knowledge retrieval","source evidence"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/ai-help/aiHelpService.ts","supabase/functions/ai-help/index.ts","supabase/functions/ai-help/assistantCore.ts"],"answer":"When online, a typed question is checked against verified Q&A first. If no clear catalog answer applies, the service can use relevant product documentation and reviewed source evidence to form a grounded answer. AI Help does not receive your tracker entries."},{"id":"calendar-content","category":"calendar","question":"What does the calendar show?","aliases":["What do the calendar colors mean?","Can I see progress by date?"],"keywords":["calendar","activity","status","heatmap","date"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/calendar/CalendarPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/activityHeatmap.ts","src/domain/trackers/entryPresentation.ts"],"answer":"The calendar lets you navigate dates and review tracker activity for the selected period. Its date indicators summarize scheduled opportunities and saved progress; open a date to review or update the entries available for that day. Selected-day details keep the tracker outcome separate from saved measure values. For example, a Yes/No value appears with its saved measure name and **Done** or **Not Done**, while the activity status can independently read **Completed** or **No progress**. Checklist totals use the item definition effective on that date when it reliably matches the saved value. Use the information button beside Status guide for the difference between saved outcomes and derived statuses, and how holidays, tracker periods, All Trackers, and streak qualification affect the summary."},{"id":"calendar-activity-statuses","category":"calendar","question":"What do the Calendar activity statuses mean?","aliases":["What is the difference between pending, missed, and no progress?","What do the status labels in Calendar mean?"],"keywords":["Calendar","status","pending","missed","completed","historical"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/activityStatus.ts","src/features/calendar/CalendarPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/entryPresentation.ts"],"answer":"Completed means a saved recorded check-in met the configured completion rule, but completion does not always mean it qualifies for a streak. Partial and No progress are saved outcomes; Skipped is an intentional saved outcome. Pending, Missed, Upcoming, Rest day, Outside period, Historical entry, Holiday, Tracker inactive, and No active trackers are derived from saved data and date, schedule, mode, or tracker context. Standard Mode treats holidays as neutral, while Strict Mode still requires activity on an active date. Rest day can also describe an in-period date outside the tracker’s schedule; dates before the effective start or after a deadline are Outside period. The Status guide’s information button explains these distinctions. A status is separate from the saved measure name and value: for example, a Yes/No false value can appear as “Status: Not Done” alongside **No progress**, while a true value can appear as “Status: Done” alongside **Completed** when its success rule qualifies. False values remain visible and missing values are not invented. In All Trackers, all completed outcomes show Completed, while mixed recorded outcomes with any partial or zero-progress tracker show Partial. A recorded zero on one tracker cannot override positive progress on another; all-zero recorded outcomes remain No progress. Missing check-ins retain their Pending, Missed, or Upcoming meaning. Mixed statuses are marked on the cell and selecting the date shows each tracker’s result. The summary and saved-entry count use that same tracker scope. Selecting one tracker, including a paused or archived tracker, shows its retained activity."},{"id":"calendar-inspect-past-date","category":"calendar","question":"How do I inspect tracker activity on a past date?","aliases":["Can I open a previous day in Calendar?","Where can I see what happened on a particular date?"],"keywords":["Calendar","past date","select date","activity"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/calendar/CalendarPage.tsx","src/features/calendar/CalendarPage.test.tsx","src/domain/trackers/entryPresentation.ts"],"answer":"Open Calendar, navigate to the month, and select the date. The selected-day panel shows each tracker’s derived outcome separately from its recorded values. Saved measure names are retained; Yes/No values read **Done** or **Not Done**, including false answers. Checklist values show “N of M checked” when the date-effective definition is reliable, and otherwise show the checked count without a guessed total. For an eligible date, choose Add check-in or Edit check-in to open the shared editor with that date selected; ineligible dates explain why editing is unavailable."},{"id":"calendar-rest-day","category":"calendar","question":"How do rest days appear in Calendar?","aliases":["Does Calendar show unscheduled tracker days?","What status does an off day have?"],"keywords":["Calendar","rest day","unscheduled","tracker schedule"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/activityStatus.ts","src/features/calendar/CalendarPage.tsx"],"answer":"In Standard Mode, an in-period date excluded by the active tracker’s schedule is a Rest day. Strict Mode makes every in-period date an opportunity, including schedule rest days. Dates before the effective start or after the deadline are Outside period, not Rest days. Saved check-ins remain visible on rest days and outside the active period."},{"id":"calendar-zero-activity","category":"calendar","question":"Does a recorded zero count as activity in Calendar?","aliases":["Is zero different from no check-in on the calendar?","Why is my zero entry not marked completed?"],"keywords":["Calendar","zero","quantity","recorded","success rule"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/activityStatus.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.ts"],"answer":"A saved zero is a recorded value, so it is different from an empty date. Whether the day is Completed depends on the tracker’s success rule; zero may be recorded without qualifying, and the Calendar can show No progress."},{"id":"calendar-holiday-entry","category":"calendar","question":"Does a saved check-in stay visible on a holiday?","aliases":["Does marking a holiday hide progress already recorded?","Can a holiday date still show my check-in?"],"keywords":["Calendar","holiday","saved check-in","retain","workspace"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/activityStatus.ts","src/features/calendar/CalendarPage.tsx"],"answer":"Yes. The selected-day details and History retain saved check-ins. Standard Mode’s holiday marker can appear alongside the saved outcome; Strict Mode still requires activity, so a missing past check-in can be Missed on a holiday."},{"id":"heatmap-normalized","category":"calendar","question":"What does the Insights heatmap measure?","aliases":["How are the heatmap colors calculated?","Does one heatmap shade mean one check-in?"],"keywords":["heatmap","eligible opportunities","qualifying check-ins","percent","Insights"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/activityHeatmap.ts","src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.tsx"],"answer":"For each date, the heatmap compares check-ins meeting each tracker’s Streak Rule with eligible opportunities and colors the result by that day’s percentage. It describes streak qualification, not success rate. In an all-tracker view, it combines opportunity counts across active trackers while applying each tracker’s Standard or Strict Mode rules."},{"id":"calendar-versus-history","category":"calendar","question":"Why does Calendar show dates that I do not see in History?","aliases":["What is the difference between Calendar and History?","Why is an empty date on Calendar missing from my History list?"],"keywords":["Calendar","History","activity status","saved check-ins","missing"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/calendar/CalendarPage.tsx","src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx"],"answer":"Calendar summarizes tracker status across selected dates, including pending, missed, holiday, and rest days. History lists saved check-ins and holidays in its selected range, with a separate recent missing-opportunity review; an empty calendar date is not necessarily a saved history entry."},{"id":"skipped-vs-unchecked","category":"check-ins","question":"What is the difference between a skipped and unchecked day?","aliases":["Is skipping the same as leaving a day blank?","What does an unchecked date mean?","What is the difference between skipped and not checked?"],"keywords":["skipped","unchecked","absent","missing check-in","outcome"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/missingCheckIns.ts","src/domain/trackers/types.ts","src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx"],"answer":"A skipped day is an explicitly saved check-in marked as skipped. An unchecked past date has no saved entry and is shown as Missed only if it was a required opportunity. A saved recorded check-in that fails its success rule remains distinct: it appears as Partial when it has positive progress, or No progress when it does not. Missed is derived and is never saved automatically."},{"id":"edit-past-checkin","category":"check-ins","question":"Can I edit a past check-in?","aliases":["Can I change yesterday’s progress?","How do I correct an old entry?"],"keywords":["history","edit","past date","check-in","values"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx","src/features/today/TodayPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","supabase/migrations/20261111000100_tracker_streak_rules_v8.sql"],"answer":"Yes, for an active, non-deleted tracker and a valid date within its configured start and deadline (or today when no deadline is set). In Calendar, select the date and choose Edit check-in; in History, open the saved entry or choose one tracker before adding a missing date. Both open the shared editor for that date, where you can update its values and note or clear it with confirmation. Paused, completed, archived, and deleted trackers cannot be opened in the shared editor; archived and Bin history are read-only. A brief notice explains that past edits can update XP, streaks, and achievements. Rewards and derived results use the activity date and are reconciled when the account syncs; offline estimates stay provisional until then."},{"id":"clear-checkin","category":"check-ins","question":"What happens if I clear a check-in?","aliases":["Can I undo a check-in?","What happens if I clear yesterday’s progress?"],"keywords":["clear","delete","history","missing","re-record","check-in"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/shared/ClearCheckInAction.tsx","src/db/localRepository.ts","src/domain/trackers/missingCheckIns.ts"],"answer":"Clearing removes the saved check-in from current progress calculations. If that date was a past opportunity, it can then appear in missing check-in review. You can record the date again by creating a new check-in."},{"id":"numeric-zero-vs-empty","category":"check-ins","question":"Is entering zero different from leaving a number blank?","aliases":["Does zero count as no progress?","Is a blank quantity treated as zero?"],"keywords":["quantity","zero","blank","observation","numeric"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/analytics.ts","src/features/shared/TrackerEntryFields.tsx","src/domain/trackers/schema.ts"],"answer":"Yes. Zero is a recorded numeric value and can be included in observations. A blank field is not a numeric observation. Whether a recorded zero qualifies as a successful check-in depends on the tracker’s success rules."},{"id":"mark-missed","category":"check-ins","question":"What happens when I mark a check-in as skipped?","aliases":["Is marking a day missed different from leaving it blank?","Does Mark as skipped break my streak?"],"keywords":["mark as skipped","skipped","outcome","unchecked","streak"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/types.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/features/today/TodayPage.tsx"],"answer":"Mark as skipped saves an intentional skipped outcome for that date. It is not the same as a derived Missed date or a saved No progress result. On a required opportunity, it does not qualify for a streak. Leaving a date unchecked creates no saved entry; after a required date elapses, it can appear as Missed."},{"id":"custom-checkin-fields","category":"check-ins","question":"What are custom check-in fields?","aliases":["Can I add a note to a check-in?","Do notes count toward goal progress?"],"keywords":["notes","custom fields","context","measure","goal progress"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/trackers/TrackerConfigurationEditor.tsx","src/features/shared/TrackerEntryFields.tsx","src/domain/trackers/types.ts","src/features/shared/TrackerEntryFields.test.tsx"],"answer":"Custom check-in fields add context to an entry, such as a note or selected answer. They are separate from tracker measures and are not used as numeric goal totals. Once a field has saved values, its label, type, options, and required setting are protected so old answers keep their meaning. Retire it to hide it from future forms; its old value remains visible and is preserved when editing that entry."},{"id":"checkin-types","category":"check-ins","question":"What kinds of values can I record in a tracker?","aliases":["Can I track a number or a yes/no habit?","What measure types are available?"],"keywords":["Yes/No","quantity","duration","checklist","measures","recorded values"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/types.ts","src/features/trackers/trackerSetupSchema.ts","src/features/trackers/TrackerConfigurationEditor.tsx","src/features/shared/TrackerEntryFields.tsx"],"answer":"Every measure, including the primary measure, can use Yes/No, Quantity, Duration, or Checklist values. Yes/No is entered and displayed as **Done** or **Not Done**; Quantity and Duration record numbers; Checklist stores each named item's checked state. New primary-measure names default to **Status**, **Progress**, **Time Spent**, and **Items** for those four types, respectively, but names are saved labels, not status values. A secondary measure starts with a generic **Measure N** name. Once saved, a measure's type is locked; once it has history, its name is also locked. Checklist item IDs and labels stay fixed after history exists so past checked states are not reinterpreted. Retire the measure and add a new one to track something differently."},{"id":"checkin-empty-versus-zero-status","category":"check-ins","question":"Why can a saved zero show no progress instead of a missed day?","aliases":["Is a zero entry treated as unchecked?","How does Calendar distinguish zero from no check-in?"],"keywords":["zero","no progress","missed","saved entry","activity status"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/activityStatus.ts","src/features/calendar/CalendarPage.tsx"],"answer":"A saved zero is still a check-in, not a missed day. Calendar evaluates it against the tracker’s success rule and may show No progress; if the rule explicitly accepts zero, it can show Completed. Missed means an elapsed required opportunity has no active saved check-in. An open opportunity today is Pending, and a future opportunity is Upcoming."},{"id":"checkin-resave-same-date","category":"check-ins","question":"What happens if I save a check-in again for the same date?","aliases":["Can a tracker have two check-ins on one day?","Does saving another entry replace my check-in for that date?"],"keywords":["same date","edit","save","latest revision","check-in"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/db/localRepository.ts","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts"],"answer":"The app keeps one active check-in per tracker and date. Saving again updates that date’s entry, and calculations use the latest live revision rather than adding a second daily record."},{"id":"checkin-note-vs-measure","category":"check-ins","question":"Does a check-in note count as a measure value?","aliases":["Can a note contribute to my numeric goal?","Are custom answers included in tracker statistics?"],"keywords":["note","custom field","measure","metric","goal progress"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/trackers/TrackerConfigurationEditor.tsx","src/features/shared/TrackerEntryFields.tsx","src/domain/trackers/analytics.ts"],"answer":"No. A note or custom check-in answer adds context to the entry. Goal calculations and measure statistics use tracker measure values, not those custom fields."},{"id":"guest-mode","category":"getting-started","question":"Can I use ProgressTracker as a guest?","aliases":["Do I need an account to start tracking?","What happens to guest data?"],"keywords":["guest","account","local storage","sign in","tracker"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/auth/AuthProvider.tsx","src/db/localRepository.ts","src/features/auth/AuthPage.tsx","src/features/auth/AuthProvider.test.tsx"],"answer":"You can use ProgressTracker without signing in. Guest tracker data is stored locally in the browser on that device. Signing in enables account synchronization, but guest data does not automatically appear on another device."},{"id":"create-tracker","category":"getting-started","question":"How do I create a tracker?","aliases":["How do I start tracking a habit?","Where do I add a new tracker?"],"keywords":["create","setup","habit","goal","schedule","measure"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/trackers/TrackerSetupPage.tsx","src/features/trackers/TrackerSetupPage.test.tsx","src/features/trackers/trackerSetupSchema.ts","src/features/trackers/TrackerConfigurationEditor.tsx"],"answer":"Open Trackers and choose Create tracker. Give it a name, choose the tracker kind and measures, then set its schedule and active dates. For a goal, open Plan targets and pace to set a daily target or a total to reach by a deadline. The target and deadline in that section are also used by the goal plan. Save the form to begin using it. Every measure supports Yes/No, Quantity, Duration, or Checklist values. The new primary measure defaults to **Status** for Yes/No, **Progress** for Quantity, **Time Spent** for Duration, and **Items** for Checklist. These are editable names; while setting up a new tracker, changing the type updates the default name unless you already edited it. Added secondary measures start with a generic name such as **Measure 2** and Quantity type. Names are saved with the tracker; older trackers retain their existing names, and a measure with history cannot be renamed. New trackers default to using the Success Rule for streaks; choose a custom Streak Rule in More options when streak progress should follow a different condition. Existing trackers keep their original streak behavior until explicitly changed."},{"id":"daily-vs-cumulative-goal","category":"goals","question":"What is the difference between daily and cumulative goals?","aliases":["How does cumulative progress work?","Does my goal target reset every day?"],"keywords":["daily plan","cumulative plan","target","allocations","progress"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/domain/trackers/allocationPreview.ts","src/domain/trackers/goalPlanning.test.ts","src/features/goals/GoalsPage.tsx"],"answer":"A daily plan sets a target for each planned day. A cumulative plan sets a total amount to reach across its date range, with progress allocated across the plan. Which model applies depends on the saved goal plan."},{"id":"cumulative-plan-rebalancing","category":"goals","question":"How does my cumulative goal rebalance its daily plan?","aliases":["Why did my planned amount change after a check-in?","Does yesterday’s planned work carry into today?","How do manual daily allocations work?"],"keywords":["cumulative goal","planned","completed","manual allocation","rebalance","deadline"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/allocationPreview.ts","src/domain/trackers/allocationPreview.test.ts","src/features/goals/CumulativeAllocationPreview.tsx","src/features/goals/CumulativeAllocationPreview.test.tsx","src/services/supabase/syncEngine.test.ts","supabase/migrations/20261107000100_tracker_manual_goal_allocations_v5.sql"],"answer":"The plan calculates remaining work from the goal target minus active saved incremental check-ins. It keeps completed work separate from planned work. Manual labels come only from saved per-date Manual override keys; generated Auto values are recalculated and never copied into that map. While today is still open, a Manual allocation is fixed and only its outstanding part (planned amount minus work already completed today) reserves remaining work. After today is recorded or skipped, it is closed: its saved Manual amount remains visible for historical comparison but no longer reserves work. A deleted entry reopens today if it is still eligible. After a date passes, its planned amount stays in schedule history, but only the check-in value affects future allocations. Remaining work is split deterministically across eligible scheduled automatic dates through the deadline. If future Manual reservations exceed the remaining goal, their values stay unchanged and the schedule reports the over-allocation. If no automatic dates remain, it reports the unallocated work. Older saved schedules may not distinguish generated values from manual edits; they require an explicit choice to keep future legacy values as Manual or use the recalculated plan. You can reset one Manual date or, with confirmation, reset future Manual overrides. Dates before the goal's effective start are outside the plan; explicit backdated starts can include entries before the tracker was created."},{"id":"milestones","category":"goals","question":"How are milestones calculated?","aliases":["When is a milestone reached?","What does a linked milestone mean?"],"keywords":["goal","milestone","target","progress","linked measure","total quantity","single day","successful days","streak","challenge day","checklist"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/milestones.ts","src/domain/trackers/types.ts","src/domain/trackers/schema.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/domain/trackers/ruleVersions.ts","src/features/trackers/TrackerConfigurationEditor.tsx","src/features/trackers/MilestoneProgressList.tsx","src/features/goals/GoalsPage.tsx","src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx","src/features/calendar/CalendarPage.tsx","src/services/supabase/syncEngine.ts","supabase/migrations/20261113000100_tracker_typed_milestones_v9.sql"],"answer":"A milestone's saved type defines what its target measures. Total quantity sums one numeric measure over eligible active-period check-ins; single-day quantity compares the best day; successful days use the Success Rule effective on each date; longest streak uses the Streak Rule effective on each date; challenge day follows the configured Calendar Days or Effective Days count; and a measure completion count matches a Yes/No or Checklist condition. Progress is recalculated from saved entries, so historical edits and deletions update it. Older milestones without a type retain their original best-single-observation meaning until the user converts them. Displayed completion follows saved activity and its applicable rules; confirmed milestone XP separately requires individually eligible check-ins after the progression cutover. A reached date is shown when it can be derived reliably, and reaching a milestone does not by itself complete the overall goal."},{"id":"goal-deadline","category":"goals","question":"Can a goal have a deadline?","aliases":["How does a goal deadline work?","What happens when a goal’s end date passes?"],"keywords":["goal","deadline","cumulative","active period","target"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/features/trackers/GoalPlanningEditor.tsx","src/domain/trackers/goalPlanning.test.ts"],"answer":"Yes. The deadline is a tracker setting shared by the goal form and Plan targets and pace. A cumulative plan uses that date to bound its planned range; progress and pacing use the scheduled dates through the deadline, and dates after it are not included in cumulative progress."},{"id":"complete-goal","category":"goals","question":"When is a goal complete?","aliases":["How do I know I reached my goal target?","Does reaching a milestone complete the goal?"],"keywords":["goal","completed","target","progress","milestone"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/goals/GoalsPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/domain/trackers/goalPlanning.test.ts"],"answer":"The goal plan reports its target as complete when no planned work remains. The Goals page also shows the tracker’s saved status, so the displayed status can depend on both the goal state and plan. A milestone is a checkpoint within a plan; reaching one does not by itself mean the overall target is complete."},{"id":"goal-daily-missing","category":"goals","question":"How does a daily goal plan treat a missing date?","aliases":["Does a missed day count as meeting my daily target?","What happens to a daily target when I do not check in?"],"keywords":["daily goal","missing","missed","target","schedule"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/domain/trackers/goalPlanning.test.ts"],"answer":"A past scheduled date without a usable check-in is treated as missed in the daily plan. Today remains pending while it is still open, and rest days, holidays, and future dates are shown separately rather than as missed opportunities."},{"id":"goal-cumulative-snapshot","category":"goals","question":"Do snapshot check-ins add together toward a cumulative goal?","aliases":["Are repeated snapshot values summed for a total goal?","Which entries count toward cumulative progress?"],"keywords":["cumulative goal","snapshot","incremental","total progress"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/features/trackers/GoalPlanningEditor.tsx","src/domain/trackers/goalPlanning.test.ts"],"answer":"No. Cumulative progress sums entries configured as incremental. Snapshot values describe a level at a point in time and are not added together across dates."},{"id":"goal-clearing-entry","category":"goals","question":"Does clearing a check-in change goal progress?","aliases":["Will a deleted entry reduce my goal total?","Does removing a historical check-in recalculate the goal?","Can clearing a check-in change my goal progress?","Will my goal total go down if I clear an entry?","Does removing a check-in update the Goals page?"],"keywords":["goal progress","clear check-in","delete entry","recalculate"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/db/localRepository.ts","src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx"],"answer":"Goal progress is calculated from active saved entries, so clearing a check-in can change the displayed progress or pacing. The effect depends on the plan and whether that entry contributes a qualifying value."},{"id":"goal-target-change","category":"goals","question":"What happens if I change a goal target?","aliases":["Does editing my target change saved check-ins?","Will a new goal target recalculate my plan?"],"keywords":["goal target","edit plan","recalculation","saved progress"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/goals/GoalsPage.tsx","src/features/trackers/GoalPlanningEditor.tsx","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts"],"answer":"The plan and its remaining pace are recalculated against the new target and existing saved progress. Changing the target does not rewrite the check-ins themselves."},{"id":"goal-metric-unit","category":"goals","question":"Where does a goal’s unit come from?","aliases":["How does a goal know whether progress is pages or minutes?","Can I choose a different unit for goal progress?"],"keywords":["goal","measure","unit","metric","quantity"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/goals/GoalsPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/features/trackers/GoalPlanningEditor.tsx"],"answer":"The goal uses the unit of its linked tracker measure. Choose or edit the measure’s unit in tracker configuration; the goal plan displays values in that unit rather than converting them. A separate elapsed-time label on deadline goals uses calendar months and remaining days from the active start date; it does not convert the measure, target, or saved progress."},{"id":"history-includes","category":"history","question":"What does History include?","aliases":["What can I see in History?","Why does History not show every date?","Where can I review saved check-ins?"],"keywords":["saved entries","historical","holidays","missing check-ins","date","values"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/missingCheckIns.ts","src/features/history/HistoryPage.test.tsx"],"answer":"History shows saved check-ins and their recorded values for past dates, along with workspace holidays in the selected date range. Each saved measure name labels its value; Yes/No values read **Done** or **Not Done**, while the entry outcome is shown separately. Checklist values show the checked-item count as items done. You can open an entry to edit it or choose a tracker and date to add a missing check-in; both use the shared check-in editor. It also offers a missing check-in review for unresolved opportunities in the previous seven completed days. Dates that were not tracking opportunities are not shown as missing, and today is not treated as overdue."},{"id":"history-clear-note","category":"history","question":"Does clearing a check-in remove its note?","aliases":["Does clearing remove a check-in note?","What happens to a note when I clear its check-in?","Is the note kept if I delete an old entry?"],"keywords":["clear check-in","note","history","deleted entry"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx","src/db/localRepository.ts"],"answer":"The note belongs to the saved check-in, so clearing the check-in removes it from active History along with the entry. Clearing does not provide a separate option to keep the note while removing the check-in."},{"id":"history-clear-sync","category":"history","question":"Is clearing a check-in the same as permanently erasing it everywhere?","aliases":["Does clearing permanently delete a check-in from storage?","Is a cleared entry removed from the cloud too?"],"keywords":["clear","permanent deletion","tombstone","sync","history"],"suggestible":false,"sources":["src/db/localRepository.ts","src/services/supabase/syncEngine.ts","src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx"],"answer":"Clearing removes the entry from active history on this device and queues a deletion update for account sync when available. The app uses deletion state during synchronization; clearing should not be treated as proof that every stored copy or backup has been permanently erased."},{"id":"history-reenter-cleared","category":"history","question":"Are my old values restored when I check in again after clearing?","aliases":["Can I undo a cleared check-in by logging again?","What if I want to add progress on that date after clearing it?"],"keywords":["clear","re-enter","save","check-in","date"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/db/localRepository.ts","src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx"],"answer":"No. Clearing removes the entry from active history, so its old values are not filled back into a new check-in. You can save progress for that tracker and date again by entering the values you want to record."},{"id":"history-cleared-missing","category":"history","question":"Why can a cleared date appear as a missing check-in?","aliases":["Does clearing make an old scheduled day missing?","Why did History list a date after I removed its entry?"],"keywords":["clear","missing check-in","scheduled opportunity","history"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/missingCheckIns.ts","src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx"],"answer":"The missing-check-in review looks for past opportunities without an active saved entry. After you clear an entry, a past date can qualify as missing if it is still an active opportunity under that tracker’s schedule, mode, and holiday rules."},{"id":"history-clear-streak","category":"history","question":"Does clearing a check-in affect my streak?","aliases":["Will deleting a past entry recalculate my streak?","What happens to a streak after I clear one day?"],"keywords":["clear check-in","streak","recalculation","opportunity"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/progression.ts"],"answer":"Yes, streaks are calculated from active saved entries that meet the tracker’s Streak Rule, so clearing one can change the current or longest streak. The result depends on whether that date is a counted opportunity under Standard or Strict Mode and the tracker’s schedule and holiday rules."},{"id":"history-outside-period","category":"history","question":"Why does History label an entry as outside the tracker period?","aliases":["What does Historical mean next to an old check-in?","Why is my saved entry not counted in current progress?"],"keywords":["History","historical entry","start date","deadline","active period"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/activityStatus.ts","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts"],"answer":"The entry was saved on a date outside the tracker’s current active period, which is bounded by its effective start date and deadline. History keeps the entry visible, but it does not count toward current period calculations."},{"id":"history-seven-day-review","category":"history","question":"How far back does History review missing check-ins?","aliases":["Can History find older missed dates?","Does the missing section cover the whole tracker history?"],"keywords":["History","missing check-ins","seven days","review window"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/missingCheckIns.ts"],"answer":"The missing check-in section reviews unresolved opportunities in the previous seven completed days. It is a short review window, not a list of every gap in the tracker’s history; use Calendar to inspect older dates."},{"id":"history-cleared-holiday","category":"history","question":"Can a cleared check-in on a holiday become a missing date?","aliases":["Will clearing a holiday entry create a missed check-in?","Does the missing review include holidays after I clear them?"],"keywords":["cleared check-in","holiday","missing","Strict Mode","Standard Mode"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/missingCheckIns.ts","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/domain/trackers/missingCheckIns.test.ts"],"answer":"In Standard Mode, holidays are excluded from scheduled opportunities, so a cleared holiday entry is not listed as missing. Strict Mode treats every active date, including holidays, as an opportunity; a past cleared holiday can therefore appear in the missing review."},{"id":"missing-checkins","category":"history","question":"Where can I find missing check-ins?","aliases":["How do I review missed days?","Can I find dates I forgot to log?","Where do I review missed check-ins?"],"keywords":["missing","overdue","history","schedule","past opportunity"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/missingCheckIns.ts"],"answer":"Open History and review its missing check-in section. It lists past unresolved opportunities for active trackers, based on each tracker’s active dates, schedule, Strict Mode, and workspace holidays. It does not list today as missing."},{"id":"create-holiday","category":"holidays","question":"How do I add a holiday?","aliases":["Can I mark a day as a break?","How do I add a retroactive holiday?"],"keywords":["holiday","break","date","reason","workspace"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/holidays/HolidaysPage.tsx","src/domain/holidays.ts","src/domain/holidays.test.ts"],"answer":"Open Holidays & breaks, choose a date, and save the holiday. You can add a reason and choose a past date; holidays apply across the workspace rather than to only one tracker. To change a saved holiday, open its three-dot menu and choose Edit holiday. Update the date, reason, or both. The edit keeps the same holiday record and syncs across devices when signed in."},{"id":"delete-holiday","category":"holidays","question":"What happens if I delete a holiday?","aliases":["Does removing a holiday change saved check-ins?","Can I undo a workspace break?"],"keywords":["holiday","delete","saved check-in","schedule","history"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/holidays/HolidaysPage.tsx","src/domain/holidays.ts"],"answer":"Deleting a holiday removes that date’s break from future calculations and moves it to Recently deleted holidays, where it can be restored for 30 days. When permanent deletion is enabled for the deployment, you can also confirm that action from the holiday’s three-dot menu. Any check-ins already saved for the date remain saved; deleting the holiday does not erase them."},{"id":"holidays-streaks","category":"holidays","question":"Do holidays count against my streak?","aliases":["How do holidays affect scheduled check-ins?","Does a holiday pause my tracker?","Do holidays count against my streak?"],"keywords":["holiday","streak","scheduled","strict mode","recorded entry"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/domain/holidays.ts"],"answer":"In Standard Mode, a holiday removes that date from scheduled streak opportunities. In Strict Mode, dates remain daily opportunities, so a holiday by itself does not excuse a missed day. A saved check-in remains visible in either mode; a qualifying one counts in Strict Mode. Goal plans use their own schedule rules."},{"id":"holiday-all-trackers","category":"holidays","question":"Do workspace holidays apply to every tracker?","aliases":["Can I make a holiday for just one tracker?","Is a holiday shared across my trackers?"],"keywords":["workspace holiday","all trackers","schedule","break"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/holidays.ts","src/features/holidays/HolidaysPage.tsx"],"answer":"Yes. Holidays are workspace-wide dates, not tracker-specific settings. Tracker opportunity behavior depends on mode: Standard Mode pauses scheduled opportunities, while Strict Mode counts every active date. Goal plans account for holidays according to their own planning rules."},{"id":"holiday-remove-recalculates","category":"holidays","question":"What changes when I remove a holiday?","aliases":["Does deleting a holiday make that date count again?","Will removing a holiday change my streak or statistics?"],"keywords":["holiday","remove","schedule","recalculate","streak"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/holidays.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/domain/trackers/analytics.ts"],"answer":"Removing the holiday makes the date subject to the tracker’s usual mode and schedule rules again. Calculated streaks and statistics can therefore change, but saved check-ins are not removed."},{"id":"holiday-log-progress","category":"holidays","question":"Can I record progress on a holiday?","aliases":["Are check-ins allowed during a workspace break?","Can I voluntarily log on a holiday?"],"keywords":["holiday","voluntary check-in","saved entry","calendar"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/calendar/CalendarPage.tsx","src/features/today/TodayPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/progression.ts"],"answer":"Yes. A holiday does not prevent a check-in from being saved. Calendar offers a voluntary check-in on an active tracker’s holiday, and the saved entry remains visible. In Standard Mode, the entry is saved and included in applicable metrics, but the holiday does not add a scheduled streak opportunity. In Strict Mode, the holiday remains a required opportunity, and the entry counts toward the streak only if it meets the tracker’s streak qualification."},{"id":"holiday-standard-v-strict","category":"holidays","question":"Why can a holiday be missed in Strict Mode?","aliases":["Why does Strict Mode still expect a check-in on a holiday?","Does Strict Mode pause for workspace holidays?"],"keywords":["Strict Mode","holiday","opportunity","missed","streak"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.test.ts"],"answer":"Strict Mode treats every date in the tracker’s active period as an opportunity, including holidays. Without a qualifying check-in, an elapsed holiday can break the streak. Standard Mode excludes holidays from scheduled opportunities."},{"id":"insight-tracker-cards","category":"insights","question":"What does the Your Trackers section show?","aliases":["What are the tracker cards in Insights?","What information appears on an Insights tracker card?"],"keywords":["Insights","tracker cards","current date","status","streak","latest check-in"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.tsx","src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.test.tsx","src/domain/trackers/entryPresentation.ts"],"answer":"Each active tracker card is a snapshot for the workspace-local current date. It shows today’s derived status, that tracker’s current streak and personal best, and its latest saved check-in with that entry’s date, outcome, and values. The saved measure names accompany the values; Yes/No values are shown as **Done** or **Not Done**, including false. Checklist summaries use a date-effective item total only when the saved definition reliably matches the recorded value; otherwise they show the checked count without a guessed total. A value such as **Not Done** is not itself the tracker status. These refer to separate dates and purposes."},{"id":"insight-all-trackers-streak","category":"insights","question":"What does the All Trackers streak on Insights measure?","aliases":["Is All Trackers streak the sum of tracker streaks?","How is my Perfect Day streak calculated?"],"keywords":["Insights","All Trackers streak","Perfect Day","account streak"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/progression.ts"],"answer":"It is the consecutive run of account days on which every required tracker meets its own Streak Rule, with at least one required tracker that day. It is not a sum of separate tracker streaks. Standard Mode holidays and rest days are neutral; Strict Mode dates within a tracker’s active period require a qualifying check-in. A pending current day does not prematurely break the confirmed run."},{"id":"insight-current-status","category":"insights","question":"Does an Insights tracker card show today or my latest check-in?","aliases":["What date does a tracker card represent?","Is the status on my tracker card from today or my last entry?"],"keywords":["Insights","snapshot date","current status","latest saved entry"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.tsx","src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.test.tsx","src/domain/trackers/entryPresentation.ts"],"answer":"The card’s status and streak are a snapshot as of today in your workspace time zone. The separate “Latest check-in” area shows the newest saved entry and its actual date, which may be earlier. That entry’s saved values are labeled with the saved measure names; **Done** and **Not Done** describe a recorded Yes/No value, while the card’s status describes the tracker’s derived outcome."},{"id":"insight-latest-checkin","category":"insights","question":"What does the latest check-in date on an Insights card mean?","aliases":["Does latest check-in mean I logged today?","Why is the check-in date on my card from an earlier day?"],"keywords":["latest check-in","saved entry","date","Insights"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.tsx","src/db/localRepository.ts","src/domain/trackers/entryPresentation.ts"],"answer":"It is the date of the most recent active saved check-in for that tracker. The outcome says whether the entry met the success rule that applies to that date; when a condition fails, the card names the measure, requirement, and saved value when available. The saved measure names and values remain visible, including a Boolean **Not Done** value. A recorded value and the derived tracker outcome are separate; for example, **Not Done** can accompany **No progress**. Checklist values show “N of M checked” only when the date-effective checklist definition is reliable, otherwise a count without a total. It does not imply that you checked in today. Cleared entries are excluded; if no active entry exists, the card says “No check-ins yet.”"},{"id":"insight-empty-tracker","category":"insights","question":"Why does an Insights card say no check-ins yet?","aliases":["What does “No check-ins yet” mean on my tracker?","Why is there no latest entry on a tracker card?"],"keywords":["Insights","empty tracker","no check-ins","latest entry"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.tsx","src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.test.tsx"],"answer":"There is no active saved check-in for that tracker. Today’s status is shown separately, so a holiday or rest day does not mean an unfinished check-in; it describes today’s tracking status."},{"id":"insight-streak-personal-best","category":"insights","question":"What do current streak and personal best mean on an Insights card?","aliases":["What is the personal best on my tracker card?","How are the two streak numbers on Insights different?"],"keywords":["current streak","personal best","longest streak","Insights"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.test.ts"],"answer":"Current streak is the qualifying run through today under the tracker’s Streak Rule and scheduling policy. Personal best is the longest qualifying run in its saved history. Standard Mode lets holidays and rest days preserve continuity without adding to the count; Strict Mode requires a qualifying entry on every active calendar date, including holidays and rest days."},{"id":"insight-success-streak-xp","category":"insights","question":"How do success rate, streaks, and XP differ for a selected tracker?","aliases":["Does a streak-qualified day count as successful?","Why did my tracker earn streak progress without daily XP?","Does tracker XP include account-wide rewards?"],"keywords":["Insights","Success Rule","Streak Rule","tracker XP","success rate","streak-qualified days"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/analytics/AnalyticsPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/analytics.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","supabase/migrations/20261111000100_tracker_streak_rules_v8.sql"],"answer":"Success rate counts recorded entries that meet the tracker’s Success Rule. Streak-qualified days and streak lengths use the Streak Rule effective for each date plus the schedule and holiday policy. In All Trackers, comparable counts are summed per tracker, so one calendar date can count once for each tracker. Analytics offers Last 7, 30, and 90 days, an inclusive custom date range, and All time. XP for a date range is net across confirmed and pending rewards in that range; All time uses lifetime confirmed XP plus current pending XP. Selected-tracker XP includes only rewards linked to that tracker. Account XP remains account-scoped even when a tracker is selected, and XP outside the selected tracker shows the remainder. Badge counts are lifetime scoped: All Trackers counts distinct earned badge types, while a selected tracker counts active unlock occurrences linked to its rewards."},{"id":"insight-holiday-status","category":"insights","question":"Why does today’s card status differ from my latest check-in?","aliases":["Why does Insights show a holiday when my last entry was completed?","Can the latest check-in and today’s status be different?"],"keywords":["Insights","today","holiday","latest check-in","current status"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/activityStatus.ts","src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.test.tsx"],"answer":"Today’s status and the latest saved check-in describe different dates. A holiday can be today’s workspace status while the latest check-in remains an earlier entry; the card labels that entry with its own date and outcome."},{"id":"insight-timezone-date","category":"insights","question":"Which time zone determines the date shown in Insights?","aliases":["Is the Insights snapshot date local to my workspace?","Why does the Insights date change around midnight?"],"keywords":["Insights","workspace time zone","snapshot date","midnight"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.tsx","src/db/calendarDate.ts","src/features/settings/WorkspaceTimeZone.tsx"],"answer":"Insights uses the current date in the workspace’s selected time zone. Because that date can differ from UTC or your device’s other time zone, the snapshot may change at a different midnight."},{"id":"reminder-limits","category":"notifications","question":"Do reminders arrive when the app is closed?","aliases":["Are reminders sent in the background?","Why did I not get a push notification?"],"keywords":["notification","reminder","foreground","background","push"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/notifications/ForegroundReminderMonitor.tsx","src/features/notifications/capabilities.ts"],"answer":"The current reminder monitor works while the app is open in the foreground. Background delivery depends on separate push delivery setup, so browser permission alone does not guarantee a reminder when the app is closed."},{"id":"notification-preferences","category":"notifications","question":"Where can I change notification preferences?","aliases":["How do I turn reminders on or off?","Can I change reminder settings?"],"keywords":["reminders","notifications","settings","browser permission"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/notifications/NotificationsSettings.tsx","src/features/notifications/capabilities.ts","src/features/notifications/NotificationsSettings.test.tsx"],"answer":"Open Settings and find Notifications to review the available reminder preferences and device permission status. Available controls depend on browser and device support."},{"id":"missing-checkin-reminder","category":"notifications","question":"How does the missing check-in reminder work?","aliases":["Why does Today show a missing check-in reminder?","When are overdue check-ins highlighted?"],"keywords":["Today","missing check-in","overdue","reminder","schedule"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/today/TodayPage.tsx","src/features/notifications/reminderRules.ts","src/features/notifications/ForegroundReminderMonitor.tsx","src/features/notifications/reminderRules.test.ts"],"answer":"The app can highlight unresolved opportunities for active trackers in its foreground experience, and History reviews missing opportunities from the previous seven completed days. These reminders depend on tracker schedules and active dates; archived and Bin trackers are not actionable reminders, and a reminder does not mean a saved check-in was deleted."},{"id":"reminder-previous-day-only","category":"notifications","question":"How far back does the overdue reminder look?","aliases":["Does the reminder scan all old missed days?","Will it notify me about every historical gap?"],"keywords":["overdue reminder","yesterday","historical","missed check-ins"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/notifications/ForegroundReminderMonitor.tsx","src/features/notifications/reminderRules.ts"],"answer":"The overdue reminder checks unresolved required opportunities from yesterday. It does not scan every historical date. Future opportunities are Upcoming and do not trigger overdue reminders. History separately offers a review of missing opportunities from the previous seven completed days."},{"id":"reminder-dismissal","category":"notifications","question":"Does dismissing a missing check-in reminder complete the date?","aliases":["If I close a reminder, is the check-in marked done?","Does dismissing a notification resolve the missed day?"],"keywords":["dismiss reminder","mark complete","check-in","notification"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/db/localRepository.ts","src/features/notifications/ForegroundReminderMonitor.tsx","src/features/notifications/reminderRules.ts"],"answer":"No. Dismissing a notification changes the reminder’s read state; it does not create a check-in or mark the date complete. The date’s progress status changes only when you save or edit a check-in."},{"id":"reminder-foreground-check","category":"notifications","question":"Why do reminders run only while ProgressTracker is open?","aliases":["Does the app check for reminders in the background?","Why did no reminder arrive after I closed the app?"],"keywords":["foreground","background","scheduler","reminders","app open"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/notifications/ForegroundReminderMonitor.tsx","src/features/notifications/NotificationsSettings.tsx"],"answer":"The reminder monitor evaluates reminders while the signed-in app is active. The Settings page reports that closed-app delivery still requires server-side sending and scheduling setup, so enabling device permission alone does not provide background reminders."},{"id":"reminder-timezone-quiet","category":"notifications","question":"Which time zone and quiet hours affect reminders?","aliases":["Are notification times based on my workspace time zone?","Why was a reminder delayed during quiet hours?"],"keywords":["reminder time","workspace time zone","quiet hours","schedule"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/notifications/NotificationsSettings.tsx","src/features/notifications/reminderRules.ts","src/features/notifications/ForegroundReminderMonitor.tsx"],"answer":"Reminder times use the workspace time zone. Quiet hours suppress daily and motivation reminders; overdue reminders also pause during quiet hours unless their exception is enabled."},{"id":"reminder-repeats-unresolved","category":"notifications","question":"Why can I get another reminder for the same unresolved date?","aliases":["Why did dismissing a reminder not stop later reminders?","Can reminders repeat while I have not checked in?"],"keywords":["reminder","repeats","unresolved","daily schedule","dismissal"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/notifications/ForegroundReminderMonitor.tsx","src/features/notifications/reminderRules.ts","src/db/localRepository.ts"],"answer":"Daily reminders are evaluated at their configured times while the app is active. Dismissing one marks that notification as read; it does not resolve the opportunity, so a later scheduled reminder can still appear while the check-in remains unresolved."},{"id":"local-settings","category":"settings-privacy","question":"Do my appearance and time zone settings sync?","aliases":["Will dark mode carry to another device?","Does changing my time zone sync to my account?"],"keywords":["appearance","time zone","settings","local","sync"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/settings/appearance.ts","src/features/settings/WorkspaceTimeZone.tsx","src/services/supabase/syncEngine.ts","src/features/settings/appearance.test.ts","src/features/settings/WorkspaceAppearance.test.tsx"],"answer":"Appearance is stored locally on each device. A signed-in workspace's time zone is saved to the account and synchronized between devices; guest workspaces keep it locally."},{"id":"timezone-dates","category":"settings-privacy","question":"Do check-in dates change when I change my time zone?","aliases":["Will my old entries move to a different day?","How does the workspace time zone affect tracking?"],"keywords":["time zone","calendar date","historical","check-in","local date"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/settings/WorkspaceTimeZone.tsx","src/db/calendarDate.ts","src/db/calendarDate.test.ts"],"answer":"Check-ins are stored by calendar date, so changing the workspace time zone does not shift already saved entries to another day. The selected time zone affects how dates and new daily boundaries are interpreted."},{"id":"feedback-identity-sharing","category":"settings-privacy","question":"How do I control whether maintainers see my details in feedback?","aliases":["Can I send feedback anonymously?","Where do I turn off sharing my name and email?","Does sharing apply to every support request?"],"keywords":["privacy","feedback","support","name","email","anonymous","sharing"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/settings/IdentitySharingSettings.tsx","src/features/settings/identitySharing.ts","src/features/feedback/SendFeedback.tsx","supabase/migrations/20261118000300_default_identity_sharing_to_on.sql","supabase/migrations/20261031000200_identity_sharing_privacy.sql"],"answer":"In Settings, use “Share my details with maintainers” to turn account name and email sharing on or off for eligible feedback and support requests. It is on by default when no preference has been saved, and your saved choice is account-wide. The preference is captured when a request is submitted; turning sharing off withdraws identity from stored requests where possible, while already viewed or exported information cannot be recalled. Requests submitted anonymously stay anonymous if you enable sharing later. This setting controls maintainer-facing feedback and support views; account identifiers remain in use internally for account operation."},{"id":"completion-rate","category":"statistics","question":"How is completion rate calculated?","aliases":["How do you calculate my completion percentage?","Why is my completion rate lower than expected?","What is the denominator for completion rate?"],"keywords":["percentage","consistency","scheduled opportunities","qualifying entries","denominator","analytics"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/analytics.ts","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/domain/trackers/ruleVersions.ts","src/domain/trackers/analytics.test.ts"],"answer":"For an active tracker with scheduled opportunities, the consistency percentage is the number of opportunities meeting the tracker’s Success Rule divided by the number of elapsed counted opportunities, rounded to a whole percent. A streak-only date does not increase success consistency. Standard Mode counts scheduled dates except holidays; Strict Mode counts every active date, including otherwise unscheduled dates and holidays. The current as-of date is left out when it has no entry yet. If there are no counted opportunities, the percentage is unavailable. Streak lengths use the separate Streak Rule."},{"id":"qualifying-checkin","category":"statistics","question":"What makes a check-in count as successful?","aliases":["What counts as a completed day?","Why did my check-in not count toward progress?"],"keywords":["success rule","threshold","qualifying","recorded","outcome","measure"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/domain/trackers/types.ts"],"answer":"A recorded check-in qualifies when its outcome and values meet the tracker’s configured success rules. A tracker can have multiple measures and rules, so recording something does not always mean the day qualifies. A skipped check-in is not a qualifying recorded result."},{"id":"points-and-rewards","category":"statistics","question":"How do achievement points and streak rewards work?","aliases":["Do I lose reward points if my streak resets?","What earns points in Achievements?"],"keywords":["achievements","points","reward","qualified check-in","milestone","longest streak"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/progressionModel.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/services/supabase/progressionRepository.ts","supabase/migrations/20261111000100_tracker_streak_rules_v8.sql","src/features/dashboard/AchievementsPage.tsx","src/features/dashboard/ProgressionAchievementsPage.tsx","src/features/dashboard/achievementCatalog.ts","src/features/dashboard/BadgeCelebrationDialog.tsx","src/features/dashboard/ProgressionAchievementsPage.test.tsx","src/features/dashboard/BadgeCelebrationDialog.test.tsx","supabase/tests/progression_achievements.test.sql","src/features/dashboard/LegacyAchievementsPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/schemaVersionGate.ts","supabase/migrations/20261104002200_preserve_deleted_tracker_reward_context.sql","supabase/migrations/20261104002300_add_perfect_month_and_comeback_achievements.sql","supabase/migrations/20261105000200_make_dedicated_one_time.sql","supabase/migrations/20261105000300_repeatable_activity_achievements.sql","supabase/migrations/20261105000700_require_full_consistency_window.sql","supabase/migrations/20261105000800_publish_consistency_qualification_details.sql","supabase/migrations/20261105000900_perfect_day_success_qualification.sql","supabase/migrations/20261106000100_strict_perfect_calendar_achievements.sql","supabase/migrations/20261117000100_versioned_tracker_evaluation_rules_v10.sql"],"answer":"The legacy Achievements view calculates its points from local saved history. When a build enables progression, Wins shows server-confirmed XP, level, reward history, and achievement badges. A check-in meeting the Success Rule effective for its date earns 10 XP, a Perfect Day earns 20 XP, streak milestones at 7, 14, 30, and 100 Streak Rule opportunities earn 35, 50, 100, and 200 XP, an eligible goal milestone earns 25 XP, and a completed goal earns 100 XP. For versioned trackers, milestone progress and progression resolve each date using its saved rule version; pre-v10 trackers retain their legacy definition until a rule-changing edit establishes history. Confirmed milestone XP still requires individually eligible check-ins after the progression cutover. Badges themselves add no XP. Perfect Day, Perfect Week, Perfect Month, and Perfect Year use the server-confirmed daily Success Rule effective on each date; the week requires all seven Monday-to-Sunday dates, the month every date in its actual length, and the year every date including leap day. Holidays and rest-only dates do not count as successful days, and each date needs at least one eligible successful tracker. The account time zone defines calendar dates. New period rules begin at a future complete-period cutover; older recorded awards remain historical and are not recreated under the new rules. The confirmed XP total comes from the server ledger; offline check-in estimates are provisional until synchronization confirms them. By default, Score History hides an award and its directly linked reversal when they fully cancel; choose Show reversed transactions to view the full history. This display setting does not change XP totals or levels. Level thresholds are 0, 100, 300, and 600 XP for levels 1 through 4, with each next level requiring 100 times the current level number in additional XP. Existing accounts may show one balance snapshot labeled “XP reconstructed from past activity”; it is not an itemized reward history and does not unlock achievements.\n\nFirst Step, the streak badges, Consistency Star, and Dedicated are one-time badges. Dedicated’s migration preserves its existing award and reversal history. Perfect Day repeats once per distinct qualifying date; Perfect Week, Perfect Month, and Perfect Year repeat for each distinct fully qualified calendar period; The Comeback repeats for a distinct qualifying recovery episode; Milestone Maker repeats for each distinct configured goal milestone; and Goal Crusher repeats for each distinct confirmed goal completion. These awards use server-confirmed identities, so retries do not duplicate an occurrence. Period badges are reconciled after edits and corrections; revocations remain in history, and a later valid qualification can earn a fresh occurrence. Earlier recorded periods are not awarded retroactively under the new rules.\n\nConsistency Star requires both at least 30 completed eligible opportunities and at least 80% adherence. Standard Mode treats holidays and unscheduled rest days as neutral for streaks; Strict Mode counts active-period dates as opportunities. Wins shows the server-computed eligible-day coverage and adherence separately, and does not infer either value from a client-side approximation. For Perfect Week, Month, and Year, every date must instead be a confirmed Perfect Day; neutral rest and holiday dates therefore fail that strict period. Their visible current-period progress counts only server-confirmed Perfect Days even if schedule history for other dates is incomplete; unverifiable dates are left uncounted and are not described as failures. Perfect Year shows the number of active confirmed Perfect Month awards, plus current-month Perfect Days separately. These display counts do not change the server's full-period badge eligibility checks. Comeback progress is descriptive rather than a percentage because qualification depends on a genuine missed required opportunity followed by seven consecutive qualifying opportunities on that tracker; neutral dates preserve the run and a saved skip does not start it.\n\nA newly confirmed badge occurrence can trigger a celebration. Awards with the same source date are shown together in one accessible popup; other awards remain queued. The first occurrence receives a grand celebration; ordinary repeats are subtle; award counts 5, 10, 25, 50, and each additional 100 receive a grand milestone celebration. Existing history is marked seen on initial account load and is not replayed. Acknowledgement is saved when the popup is dismissed, and event identities suppress duplicate presentations across retries and navigation. Permanent deletion offers Keep My Wins, which preserves eligible rewards and their history, or Delete Tracker and Wins, which removes only rewards linked to that tracker. If rewards cannot be safely separated, deletion stops. The progression view stays disabled unless the build sets `VITE_ENABLE_PROGRESSION_UI=true`."},{"id":"repeatable-progress-badges","category":"statistics","question":"What do Perfect Week, Month, Year, and The Comeback badges require?","aliases":["How do I earn Perfect Month?","How do I earn Perfect Year?","How do I earn The Comeback badge?"],"keywords":["Perfect Week","Perfect Month","Perfect Year","The Comeback","achievement","holiday","streak","badge"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/progressionModel.ts","src/features/dashboard/achievementCatalog.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","supabase/migrations/20261105000900_perfect_day_success_qualification.sql","supabase/migrations/20261106000100_strict_perfect_calendar_achievements.sql","supabase/migrations/20261104002300_add_perfect_month_and_comeback_achievements.sql","supabase/migrations/20261105000300_repeatable_activity_achievements.sql"],"answer":"Perfect Week requires all seven dates in a completed Monday-to-Sunday week; Perfect Month requires every date of its completed month; Perfect Year requires every date of its completed calendar year, including February 29 in a leap year. Each date must satisfy the server-confirmed Perfect Day success rule and have at least one eligible tracker with a positive target. Holidays, rest-only dates, skips, and missed required activity cannot count as successful dates. A tracker not scheduled on a date does not fail the date if another eligible tracker succeeds. These period badges can be earned again for different periods. Wins separately displays confirmed Perfect Day counts for the current week or month, and active Perfect Month awards toward the current year's 12 months. It can show confirmed partial counts when other dates cannot be verified; unknown dates remain uncounted and are not treated as failed. This display does not weaken the complete-period unlock requirements. The Comeback is earned after a qualifying tracker opportunity is followed by a genuinely missed required opportunity, then seven consecutive qualifying eligible opportunities. A saved skip does not trigger recovery, and neutral dates preserve the recovery run. These badges add no XP, and missing history is not reconstructed."},{"id":"completion-missed-dates","category":"statistics","question":"Do missed dates affect completion rate?","aliases":["Does a missed day lower my consistency percentage?","Why did my completion rate decrease after an unchecked day?"],"keywords":["completion rate","missed opportunity","denominator","consistency"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/analytics.ts","src/domain/trackers/analytics.test.ts"],"answer":"Counted opportunities contribute to the denominator, while qualifying entries contribute to the numerator. A missed counted opportunity therefore lowers the percentage. Standard Mode excludes holidays and unscheduled days; Strict Mode counts every active date."},{"id":"completion-holidays-rest-days","category":"statistics","question":"Do holidays and rest days affect completion rate?","aliases":["Are holidays included in consistency statistics?","Do unscheduled dates count in the percentage?"],"keywords":["completion rate","holidays","rest days","Standard Mode","Strict Mode"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/analytics.ts","src/domain/trackers/analytics.test.ts","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts"],"answer":"In Standard Mode, holidays and unscheduled rest days are excluded from counted opportunities. Strict Mode counts every active date, including holidays and dates outside the regular schedule. A saved qualifying check-in on a holiday can count in either mode."},{"id":"completion-no-opportunities","category":"statistics","question":"Why is a tracker’s completion rate unavailable?","aliases":["Why is there no percentage for this tracker?","What if my tracker has no counted dates yet?"],"keywords":["completion rate","no opportunities","active period","schedule"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/analytics.ts","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts"],"answer":"The percentage is unavailable when there are no counted opportunities in the selected period. This can happen before a tracker’s active period or when its schedule and mode produce no opportunities in that range."},{"id":"analytics-metric-units","category":"statistics","question":"Does Analytics combine different measure units into one total?","aliases":["Are pages and minutes added together in Analytics?","How does Insights summarize multiple kinds of values?"],"keywords":["Analytics","Insights","measures","units","observations"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/analytics.ts","src/features/analytics/AnalyticsPage.tsx"],"answer":"No. Analytics summarizes each measure separately, so values with different units are not added together. Comparable counts such as completed opportunities can be summed across trackers; the same calendar date can contribute once for each tracker. Measure values stay with their own tracker and unit."},{"id":"completion-holiday-entry","category":"statistics","question":"Does a check-in on a holiday count toward completion rate?","aliases":["If I log on a holiday, does my percentage go up?","Does holiday progress count in consistency statistics?"],"keywords":["completion rate","holiday","qualifying check-in","Strict Mode","Standard Mode"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/analytics.ts","src/domain/trackers/analytics.test.ts"],"answer":"It depends on the tracker’s mode. Standard Mode excludes holidays from counted opportunities, so a holiday entry does not affect that rate. Strict Mode counts every active date, including holidays, and a qualifying saved entry contributes to the rate."},{"id":"standard-vs-strict","category":"streaks","question":"What is the difference between Standard Mode and Strict Mode?","aliases":["Does Strict Mode count rest days?","Which days become opportunities in Strict Mode?"],"keywords":["Standard Mode","Strict Mode","schedule","daily","opportunity","holidays"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/domain/trackers/analytics.ts","src/features/trackers/TrackerConfigurationEditor.tsx"],"answer":"Standard Mode counts the tracker’s scheduled dates as opportunities and pauses over unscheduled days and holidays. Strict Mode counts every date in the active period, including unscheduled dates and holidays. A saved qualifying check-in on a holiday can still count in either mode."},{"id":"streak-statistics","category":"streaks","question":"How do streak statistics work?","aliases":["How are streaks calculated?","What counts toward my current streak?","Why did my streak reset?"],"keywords":["current streak","longest streak","qualifying check-in","schedule","strict mode","rest day","holiday"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/domain/trackers/ruleVersions.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.test.ts","supabase/migrations/20261111000100_tracker_streak_rules_v8.sql"],"answer":"Your current streak is the run of recent tracking opportunities whose entries meet the Streak Rule effective on each date. Your longest streak is the best qualifying run in the tracker’s history. A missed required opportunity can end the current run, while the longest record remains. Which dates count depends on the tracker’s schedule, Strict Mode, and holidays. Success rates and normal daily success XP use the separate Success Rule effective on each date. A versioned rule change does not reset continuity across the date boundary."},{"id":"all-trackers-streak","category":"streaks","question":"How does the All Trackers streak work?","aliases":["Is the All Trackers streak the sum of my tracker streaks?","What is an account-wide Perfect Day streak?"],"keywords":["All Trackers","account streak","Perfect Day","shared streak"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/progression.test.ts"],"answer":"It counts consecutive dates when at least one tracker has a required opportunity and every required tracker meets its own Streak Rule. It is separate from each tracker’s own streak. Standard Mode holidays and rest days are neutral; Strict Mode requires active-period dates. A known failed opportunity ends the run, while a neutral or still-pending date does not add a day or prematurely break the confirmed run."},{"id":"rest-days-streaks","category":"streaks","question":"How do rest days affect streaks?","aliases":["Do unscheduled days break a streak?","Does my schedule pause my streak?"],"keywords":["schedule","unscheduled","opportunity","strict mode","rest day"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts"],"answer":"In Standard Mode, only scheduled check-in dates are opportunities, so unscheduled rest days do not break a streak. Strict Mode treats every active date as an opportunity, including dates outside the regular schedule. Tracker start and deadline dates still bound the active period."},{"id":"streak-longest","category":"streaks","question":"What is the difference between my current streak and longest streak?","aliases":["Does losing my streak erase my record?","Why is my longest streak higher than my current streak?"],"keywords":["current streak","longest streak","record","history"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.test.ts","supabase/migrations/20261111000100_tracker_streak_rules_v8.sql"],"answer":"Your current streak describes your ongoing qualifying run. Your longest streak is the best qualifying run found in the tracker’s history, so a current streak ending does not erase that record."},{"id":"streak-skipped","category":"streaks","question":"Does marking a check-in as skipped count toward a streak?","aliases":["Is an intentionally missed entry a completed day?","Does “Marked missed intentionally” qualify for a streak?"],"keywords":["skipped","marked missed","streak","qualifying entry"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.test.ts","src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx"],"answer":"No. A Skipped entry is a saved intentional outcome, not a derived Missed date or a recorded No progress check-in. It does not qualify for a streak on a required opportunity. Standard Mode rest days and holidays are excluded from the streak; Strict Mode requires qualifying activity on every in-period date."},{"id":"streak-zero-quantity","category":"streaks","question":"Does recording zero keep a streak alive?","aliases":["Can a zero quantity value qualify for a streak?","Why did my zero entry not count toward my streak?"],"keywords":["zero","quantity","streak qualification","success rule"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.test.ts"],"answer":"A numeric zero does not qualify when a custom Streak Rule uses **Any positive value (> 0)**; any value above zero does. For a Checklist, at least one checked item qualifies. Blank or missing values do not qualify, and negative numeric values are not valid recorded progress. Other Streak Rules may treat zero differently. New v8 trackers can use the Success Rule or a separate custom rule; older trackers retain their original behavior until explicitly changed. Check the rule and schedule if the result is unexpected."},{"id":"restore-deleted-tracker","category":"trackers","question":"Can I restore a deleted tracker?","aliases":["Where do deleted trackers go?","How do I recover a tracker from the Bin?"],"keywords":["Bin","restore","deleted tracker","archive","recover"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/trackers/TrackerBinPage.tsx","src/features/trackers/TrackerLibraryPage.tsx","src/features/trackers/TrackerBinPage.test.tsx"],"answer":"Move a tracker to the Bin to keep its saved progress and plan. Choose Restore to use it again. If a restore is still in progress, the tracker stays unavailable until it finishes. Archiving is different: an archived tracker stays in your library with its history."},{"id":"bin-retention","category":"trackers","question":"What happens to a tracker after I delete it?","aliases":["Is a deleted tracker erased immediately?","How long can I restore something from The Bin?"],"keywords":["Move to Bin","Bin","Restore","Permanently Delete","Keep My Wins","Delete Tracker and Wins"],"suggestible":false,"sources":["src/features/trackers/TrackerBinPage.tsx","src/db/localRepository.ts","src/services/supabase/syncEngine.ts"],"answer":"Moving a tracker to the Bin keeps its saved progress and rewards. You can restore it while it is in the Bin. Permanently Delete cannot be undone. The confirmation explains that unsynced changes and tracker-owned history may be lost. Choose Keep My Wins to remove the tracker and its activity while preserving earned XP, badges, achievements, reward history, and appropriate tracker context. Choose Delete Tracker and Wins to remove the tracker and its activity and reverse only rewards linked to it. Other rewards and achievements stay. If rewards cannot be safely separated, the server rejects that selected policy and nothing is deleted. After confirmation, deletion is saved locally even when offline, and its Wins choice stays attached to the request while it is pending. If the server definitively rejects Delete Tracker and Wins because reward attribution is incomplete, the Bin offers an explicit confirmation to create a new Keep My Wins request; an uncertain or in-flight request cannot be changed. Pending tracker configuration and check-in operations are superseded so they cannot replay. Once online, the app fetches a fresh cloud revision and asks the owner-checked deletion RPC to delete the tracker atomically. Sync conflicts do not require repair first. The tracker is hidden locally while deletion is pending; local content and conflict UI are cleared only after the server confirms deletion. A durable server deletion ledger blocks stale writes from older versions and other devices from recreating the tracker."},{"id":"edit-tracker-history","category":"trackers","question":"Do tracker edits change historical statistics?","aliases":["What happens to old stats when I edit a tracker?","Can changing a measure change old entries?"],"keywords":["edit","historical","measure type","schedule","statistics"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/invariants.ts","src/features/trackers/TrackerConfigurationEditor.tsx","src/domain/trackers/analytics.ts","src/domain/trackers/ruleVersions.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/domain/trackers/types.ts","src/db/localRepository.ts","src/domain/trackers/historicalDependencies.ts","supabase/migrations/20261117000100_versioned_tracker_evaluation_rules_v10.sql","supabase/migrations/20261119000100_tracker_edit_sync_guards.sql"],"answer":"Rule and schedule edits can change derived success, streaks, and progress, but saved check-in values, notes, dates, and identities remain intact. Versioned trackers evaluate each date with the rule settings saved for that date. An existing measure’s type is immutable even when no check-in is visible locally; its stable ID must keep the same cloud and historical meaning. Checklist item definitions also stay fixed after history exists. All-history recalculation also checks every measure referenced by success or streak rules, goal plans, and measure milestones against each date-effective snapshot. If a measure was unavailable, retired, reactivated after a gap, changed meaning, or its historical definition cannot be proven, all-history recalculation is unavailable. Legacy trackers without date-effective snapshots cannot prove that history. Custom-field definitions on existing trackers cannot currently be added, removed, retired, reactivated, or semantically changed because their historical availability is not date-versioned. Existing custom-field values remain preserved, and position-only ordering changes are allowed."},{"id":"tracker-rule-history-choices","category":"trackers","question":"How does changing a tracker rule affect my past progress?","aliases":["What does Apply from today mean?","What happens if I recalculate all history?","Will editing a rule change my saved check-ins?"],"keywords":["tracker rule","historical rules","Apply from today","recalculate history","streak","XP"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/trackers/TrackerSetupPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/historicalDependencies.ts","src/domain/trackers/ruleVersions.ts","src/domain/trackers/types.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","supabase/migrations/20261117000100_versioned_tracker_evaluation_rules_v10.sql","supabase/migrations/20261119000100_tracker_edit_sync_guards.sql"],"answer":"For supported evaluation or measure edits on an existing tracker, choose **Apply from today**, **After the last check-in**, or **Apply to all history**. The displayed effective date uses the workspace time zone. Earlier dates retain their saved rule snapshots for forward-only edits; a check-in is evaluated using the configuration effective on its date. Structural measure changes cannot apply to all history, and Apply from today is unavailable when a same-day check-in would be reinterpreted; choose After the last check-in to start the day after the latest saved entry. If two choices resolve to the same date, they have the same effect. Apply to all history is offered only when v10 snapshots cover the full period, required inputs and reconciliation are available, and every measure referenced by the success rule, streak rule, goal plan, or measure milestone was available with the same meaning throughout that period. It is also unavailable when past successful-day or streak rewards could change. If those dependencies or their history cannot be proven, the option is disabled with a reason. Deferred changes require confirmation. Existing check-in values, notes, dates, and IDs are preserved. Milestone requirement edits and existing goal plan edits are currently blocked because their historical requirements are not versioned. Cosmetic edits do not ask for a history policy."},{"id":"archive-tracker","category":"trackers","question":"What happens when I archive a tracker?","aliases":["Does archiving delete my tracker history?","Can I restore a paused tracker?"],"keywords":["archive","pause","active","history","delete"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/trackers/TrackerLibraryPage.tsx","src/features/trackers/TrackerBinPage.tsx"],"answer":"Archiving a tracker removes it from Today and current activity while keeping its recorded history and rewards. The tracker list can show active, archived, or all trackers. When editing an archived tracker, choose whether to keep it archived or move it to active after saving. Deleting a tracker is a separate action that moves it through the app’s Bin and restore flow."},{"id":"tracker-schedules","category":"trackers","question":"How do tracker schedules work?","aliases":["Which days count as scheduled?","How do I choose tracking days?"],"keywords":["schedule","weekly","daily","weekdays","opportunity"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/features/trackers/TrackerSetupPage.tsx"],"answer":"New trackers start with Daily recurrence. You can choose Weekdays, Weekends, any non-empty Custom Days combination (including Saturday only or Sunday only), or No Recurrence. In Standard Mode, No Recurrence creates no mandatory or missed check-in days, but you can still record flexible progress from the tracker library or Calendar. The selected recurrence controls Standard Mode expected dates, consistency, and Goal Auto planning; Strict Mode treats every active date as a streak opportunity. Calendar Days stays fixed. Effective Days can count recurrence-matching activity dates or all non-holiday dates; existing records without a method retain the latter behavior. Editing a schedule on an existing tracker uses the three history choices when evaluation changes; Apply to all history is unavailable for schedule changes unless compatibility is proven, and the exact effective date is shown before confirmation."},{"id":"start-date-deadline","category":"trackers","question":"How do a tracker’s start date and deadline affect it?","aliases":["When does a tracker begin counting?","Does a deadline stop future check-ins?"],"keywords":["start date","deadline","active period","schedule","tracker"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/domain/trackers/activePeriod.test.ts","src/domain/trackers/planning.test.ts","src/features/trackers/TrackerSetupPage.tsx"],"answer":"The tracker’s active period begins on its configured start date, or its creation date in the workspace time zone when no start date is set, and ends at its deadline when one is set. A configured start date can be before tracker creation, allowing eligible past activity to be recorded. Dates outside the active period are not tracking opportunities; a deadline stops schedule-based calculations from counting later dates. An existing tracker’s start date or deadline change uses the history policy choices, but Apply to all history is disabled unless compatibility is proven. The editor shows the effective date and requires confirmation for a deferred change. Saved check-ins outside the resulting active period stay in History but do not count as opportunities."},{"id":"tracker-duration-modes","category":"trackers","question":"What is the difference between Calendar Days, Effective Days, and Ongoing?","aliases":["How does an Effective Days deadline work?","Do holidays change my tracker deadline?"],"keywords":["Calendar Days","Effective Days","Ongoing","deadline","holiday","rest day","duration"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/scheduling.ts","src/features/trackers/TrackerSetupPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/challengeDay.ts"],"answer":"Calendar Days uses the deadline you choose, and holidays or rest days do not move it. Effective Days asks for a number of counted dates and projects the deadline using the selected counting method. New scheduled trackers can count only recurrence-matching activity dates, or include every non-holiday calendar date. Existing records without a saved method keep the previous behavior of counting every date except holidays explicitly marked in ProgressTracker's calendar. Public holidays, festivals, and missed check-ins do not change eligibility; missed check-ins still consume any eligible Effective Day. Ongoing has no fixed deadline. These duration counts are separate from activity schedules, completed check-ins, and streaks. Editing an existing tracker’s duration or scheduling settings uses the three history choices; Apply to all history is disabled unless historical compatibility is proven."},{"id":"retire-measure","category":"trackers","question":"What happens when I retire a measure?","aliases":["Can I remove a measure but keep its history?","Why is an old measure still shown in History?"],"keywords":["retire","measure","old entries","history","future check-ins"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/trackers/TrackerConfigurationEditor.tsx","src/domain/trackers/types.ts","src/domain/trackers/schema.test.ts","src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx"],"answer":"Retiring a measure removes it from future check-ins while keeping its definition available to interpret older entries. Resolve any success-rule, streak-rule, goal-plan, or milestone dependency first. Measure edits use a date-effective history choice; structural changes cannot apply to all history, and cannot start today if a check-in already exists today. The editor offers After the last check-in in that case. That is why an old measure may still appear when you review historical data."},{"id":"tracker-editing","category":"trackers","question":"How do I edit a tracker?","aliases":["Where can I change a tracker’s schedule?","Can I add another measure to a tracker?"],"keywords":["edit","tracker","schedule","measures","configuration"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/trackers/TrackerLibraryPage.tsx","src/features/trackers/TrackerConfigurationEditor.tsx","src/features/trackers/TrackerSetupPage.tsx","src/features/trackers/TrackerSetupPage.test.tsx"],"answer":"Open Trackers, choose the tracker’s edit action, update its supported settings, then save. Supported rule or measure changes offer **Apply from today**, **After the last check-in**, and **Apply to all history**, with an exact effective date in the workspace time zone. Structural measure changes cannot apply to all history, and Apply from today is disabled when today’s check-in would be reinterpreted. Apply to all history is enabled only when compatibility and required historical inputs are proven. Deferred changes require confirmation; check-ins are never deleted automatically. Milestone requirement edits and existing goal plan edits are blocked until their history can be preserved safely. A rename, description, or other cosmetic edit does not show the choice. Saved check-ins remain intact, and an existing measure’s type cannot be changed."},{"id":"tracker-created-active-date","category":"trackers","question":"Does a tracker count dates before I created it?","aliases":["Does its start date include days before the tracker existed?","Why does a tracker created today start counting today?"],"keywords":["tracker creation date","start date","active period","workspace time zone"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/domain/trackers/activePeriod.test.ts"],"answer":"Yes, when you set a start date before creating the tracker. Eligible dates from that configured start through today can be recorded and edited; missing dates stay empty until you add a check-in. Without an explicit start date, the active period begins on the tracker’s creation date in the workspace time zone. Schedule, deadline, and archived status still apply."},{"id":"archived-checkin-history","category":"trackers","question":"Can I edit check-ins after archiving a tracker?","aliases":["Is archived tracker history read-only?","Does archiving keep old entries but stop edits?"],"keywords":["archived tracker","check-in","history","read-only","archive"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx","src/features/trackers/TrackerLibraryPage.tsx"],"answer":"Archiving keeps the tracker’s saved history, but its check-ins are read-only while the tracker is archived. Restore it to active status if you need to edit its check-ins again."}] as const
